-- The NeoMusic prelude: conventional names, each an ordinary definition over
-- the primitives. Read before every score; a score's own definition of any of
-- these names replaces this one. #k marks a number parameter.

-- Loudness: level multiplies, so these nest by multiplying.
vel #v x      = level v [x]            -- strength, 0..1
swell #s x    = level s [x]            -- a loudness shape, e.g. swell 1/4 -> 1
cresc #a #b x = level across a -> b [x]   -- louder across the whole group (velocity too)
dim #a #b x   = level across a -> b [x]   -- softer across the whole group

-- Pitch shapes: pitch adds, in steps.
bend #s x     = pitch s [x]            -- e.g. bend 0 -> 1, bend {0:0 1/4:1 1:0}
vibrato #d x  = pitch (d * sine 3) [x] -- depth d steps, 3 cycles a beat
cents #c x    = pitch (cents c) [x]    -- a fine offset in cents, any tuning

-- Time and tempo
hold #k x     = speed 1/k [x]          -- a fermata: held k times as long
rit #r x      = speed 1 -> r [x]       -- slow to r times the tempo
accel #r x    = speed 1 -> r [x]       -- speed up to r times the tempo
swing #s x       = speed cycle {1/2:(1/(2*s)) 1/2:(1/(2*(1 - s)))} [x]       -- long-short eighths, share s
swingPer #p #s x = speed cycle {(p/2):(1/(2*s)) (p/2):(1/(2*(1 - s)))} [x]   -- swing over p beats
staccato x    = gate 1/2 [x]           -- each note sounds half its length
legato x      = gate 3/2 [x]           -- each note rings into the next

-- Pitch
up #n x       = [x + n]                -- transpose by n steps
octave x      = up 12 [x]              -- up an octave in 12-EDO

-- Humanizing: players are never exactly even. noise seed rate is a repeatable
-- random signal (rate knots a beat, joined by lines, within -1..1); start holds
-- a signal's value through each note. Neighbouring notes get related values,
-- as a player's do. The seed picks the pattern: give each part its own.
vary #seed #a x  = level across (1 - a * (1 - start (noise seed 3)) / 2) [x]   -- each note up to a softer
loose #seed #b x = lag across (b * (1 + noise (seed + 7919) 3) / 2) [x]       -- each note up to b beats late
drift #seed #c x = pitch across (cents (c * noise (seed + 15838) 1/2)) [x]    -- intonation wandering within c cents
humanize #seed x = loose seed 1/48 [vary seed 0.15 [x]]                       -- both, gently

-- Repetition
twice x       = [x]*2
echo #n #v x  = [x vel v [x]]*n        -- x, then a quieter copy, n times
